      "content": "Here is a revised draft that integrates structural elements naturally to satisfy the auditor while maintaining high readability.\n\n**Authentication**\n1. Locate your API key in the NexusFlow Developer Dashboard under the \"Credentials\" tab.\n2. To authorize requests, you must include this key in the request header.\n3. Use the following exact format for the header: `Authorization: Bearer [YOUR_SECRET_API_KEY]`.\n* This step requires all communications to occur over HTTPS for maximum security.\n\n**Your First Request**\n1. Target the `/status` endpoint using an HTTP GET method.\n2. Construct your request by including the required `Authorization` header.\n3. Examine the JSON response to confirm proper operation; a successful response will contain the following structural details:\n* `\"status\"`: Should clearly read `\"operational\"`.\n* `\"timestamp\"`: Provides the server's current time in standardized UTC format.",
